    fix(frontend): reveal the blocked reason instantly, not with an animation (commander's 19:48 rule)
    
    HJ-P1's discriminating test showed scrollIntoView({behavior:"smooth"}) sampled scrollY=0 six
    times under this machine's mobile emulation while the same element moved 0 -> 650 instantly
    five times out of five.  A reason that only arrives if the compositor animates is not a
    testable product behaviour, so the reveal is now instant and the gate's wait is a guard
    (1.5s) rather than an animation timer.  killZ1 re-anchored to the new line: still KILLED.

